     4. Use of the source
 
     The source code can be used under the following conditions:
       - The source code or part of it may not be used in a commercial 
         program (= any program you have to pay money to use).
       - If you release a program that uses the source or part of it, you
         MUST:
           - release the FULL source code to the program too - under the
             same terms as these (and send a copy directly to us at 
             2:238/64.0 or pop@poboxes.com).
           - NOT call it Portal of Power.
           - keep the original Copyright message.
       - If you find any bugs/make enhancements/changes in the source code
         you should send the changes to us, so we can coordinate the
         development of "the original Portal of Power"


     3. Use of Portal

     Use of Portal requires you to send a postcard (and NOT just a piece of
     paper - but a real postcard, with a picture on one side, and a small
     greeting on the other....) to each of the five members of the Portal
     Team. If used commercially, a donation of $50 for AIDS research is
     also REQUIRED! The Portal Team can at any time ask of a commercial
     system to see the receipt of paid donation.
     If one or more of the following items are true for you, the use of
     Portal on your system is considered commercial:

       - You have 4 or more lines.
       - Your system (phone bill, equipment etc.) is run/paid by/for a
         company, corporation, school, church, government, foundation or
         any other kind of organization for the sole purpose of running a
         BBS.
       - You are running a pay system.
       - Extra is charged by the phone company when calling your system.
       - You are a software author, writing a BBS/utilities for a BBS or
         software for FidoNet (or a compatible network) that can't be used
         freely by the same people that can use Portal freely.

     4. Warranty?

     You must be kidding - we offer Portal almost for free (see section 3:
     Use of Portal), so the only warranty you get is that when installed it
     will use a minimum of 1 MB of your harddisk space. The Portal Team can
     under no circumstances be made responsible for ANYTHING that happens
     to/on your system (loss of data, lost profit, damage to your equipment
     etc.).
